  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is structure-linked annotation resources growing in content while becoming easier to query computationally. CATH and TED broaden superfamily number and diversity by integrating PDB and AlphaFold structures. GPCRdb adds structure and ligand data, including Boltz-2 and AlphaFold2-Multimer models. ThermoMutDB 2.0 uses LLM-plus-rule curation to add 1763 thermostability mutation entries with mutant structural models. PDBe extends literature-mined residue annotations, links MD data via MDposit, adds MOLE pore analyses, and offers API and MCP access. MobiDB adds a versioned REST API, an MCP server, Nextflow workflows and static datasets. The Chemical Probes Portal, with 26% more curated probes, is expert-reviewed and fits this thread more loosely.",
